NEARS-3413 QA finding: reply compose bar never renders for an admin-sentinel
conversation once it has >=1 message (blocks AC3).

Root cause (confirmed by reading + live API call):
- VendorApp/lib/features/chat/screens/chat_screen.dart gates the entire compose
  Row (image-pick / text field / send button) behind:
    (chatController.messageModel != null &&
     (chatController.messageModel!.status! || chatController.messageModel!.messages!.isEmpty))
  else branch renders `const SizedBox()` — no fallback compose UI at all.
- `status` comes verbatim from the backend's `messages()` endpoint
  (Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/Vendor/ConversationController.php), which
  computes it as "does the vendor have an active order with this participant" —
  and has NO branch at all for receiver_type/sender_type == 'admin', so it always
  falls through to `else { $order = 0; }` => status:false for every admin thread.
- The only escape hatch is `messages.isEmpty` (first message ever). Every
  subsequent app-open of that same admin thread has status:false AND
  messages non-empty => compose permanently hidden. There is no "active order"
  concept for a Nears Support thread, so this can never self-resolve.

Live proof — curl against the isolated QA backend (multi_food_db_qa3413, port 8413),
vendor Ahmed Khan (ahmed.khan@demo.com), conversation_id=65 (the only real
admin-sentinel fixture in the seed data, 3 vendor-authored messages):

  $ curl -s "http://127.0.0.1:8413/api/v1/vendor/message/details?conversation_id=65&limit=10&offset=1" \
      -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" -H "vendorType: owner"
  {
    "total_size": 3,
    ...
    "status": false,
    ...
  }

Screenshot bug-admin-compose-bar-hidden.png (= ac2-chatscreen-vendor-initiated.png)
shows the live ChatScreen for this exact conversation: AppBar "Nears Support" +
badge render correctly (the ticket's own fix), full message history renders, but
there is NO text field / send button / image-attach icon anywhere on screen —
confirmed by a full-screen screenshot down to the bottom safe area.

Regression cross-check: the SAME gate also hides the compose bar for a
delivery_man thread with no active order (Ali Hassan, all vendor-authored,
screenshot regression-deliveryman-chat.png) — so the underlying order-gate
mechanism is pre-existing, generic product behavior, NOT introduced by this
diff. What IS new/in-scope: AC3 explicitly promises "sending a reply... succeeds"
for admin threads, and that promise is unreachable via the UI for any admin
thread beyond its first message, because no "order" concept can ever apply to a
Nears Support conversation. The dispatch-layer fix in chat_service.dart
(processSendMessage's new admin branch) is correct but unreachable — there is no
send button to tap.
